ative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a07fc94f-5b6d-5ea9-93c2-7e82f2229b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a07fc94f-5b6d-5ea9-93c2-7e82f2229b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503901} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe4c120-0640-5e64-a81c-759b876005de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a26b65ff-d0b9-55fd-88b5-aeb6bb366617" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}={x}^{8/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{8}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{8/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{8/5+1}}{(\\frac{8}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{13/5}}{(\\frac{13}{5})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{13}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{13/5})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{13}\\cdot \\frac{13}{5}{x}^{13/5-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{8/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fi